# Armor
# Source: The (mostly) Complete Dragon Magazine Compendium - Arms and Equipment (compendium pp. 1198-1270).
# DESC ends with the original Dragon/Dungeon Magazine issue and article. SOURCEPAGE = compendium PDF page.

Resin Suit	PROFICIENCY:ARMOR|Resin Suit	TYPE:ArmorProfLight.ArmorType_Light.Armor.Light.Suit.Standard	COST:250	WT:20	ACCHECK:-4	MAXDEX:3	SPELLFAILURE:25	BONUS:COMBAT|AC|4|TYPE=Armor	BONUS:VAR|ArmorCheckPenalty|4	SOURCEPAGE:p.1216	DESC:A kaorti resin suit consists of thin strips of alchemically treated resin wrapped fully around the body, similar to a mummy's wrappings. Many kaorti resin suits also feature complex ridges and designs on the legs and arms. Non-kaorti can wear resin suits, but for most creatures contact with the resin results in rashes or hives (these hives have no in-game effect). A kaorti in a resin suit is protected from the natural world and does not suffer the effects of its Material vulnerability. [Dungeon #118 (Shadow of the Abyss)]
Twisted Silk	PROFICIENCY:ARMOR|Twisted Silk	TYPE:ArmorProfLight.ArmorType_Light.Armor.Light.Suit.Standard	COST:400	WT:15	ACCHECK:0	MAXDEX:7	SPELLFAILURE:5	BONUS:COMBAT|AC|3|TYPE=Armor	SOURCEPAGE:p.1216	DESC:Rare and valuable, twisted silk armor uses silk wound around strands of mithral to generate protection with very little weight. It superficially resembles a very well made form of padded armor but offers much greater defense. The silk keeps it silent and the twisted strands are surprisingly durable. [Dragon #348 (Class Acts – Mountain Ghosts)]
Eagle Knight Armor	PROFICIENCY:ARMOR|Eagle Knight Armor	TYPE:ArmorProfMedium.ArmorType_Medium.Armor.Medium.Suit.Standard	COST:165	WT:25	ACCHECK:-2	MAXDEX:4	SPELLFAILURE:20	BONUS:COMBAT|AC|3|TYPE=Armor	BONUS:VAR|ArmorCheckPenalty|2	SOURCEPAGE:p.1216	DESC:This armor consists of cloth woven with eagle feathers and placed over multiple layers of padding. The coif, which is decorated as an eagle's head, frames the knight's face with a beaklike visor. The leggings are often fashioned with decorative talons. Note: See the Maztican Armor sidebar for more information. [Dragon #315 (Maztica – The New (Fantasy)])
Jaguar Knight Armor	PROFICIENCY:ARMOR|Jaguar Knight Armor	TYPE:ArmorProfMedium.ArmorType_Medium.Armor.Medium.Suit.Standard	COST:165	WT:25	ACCHECK:-2	MAXDEX:4	SPELLFAILURE:20	BONUS:COMBAT|AC|3|TYPE=Armor	BONUS:VAR|ArmorCheckPenalty|2	SOURCEPAGE:p.1216	DESC:Jaguar knight armor is made from the pelts of one or more jaguars placed over layers of padding. The coif, which is actually made from the skull of a jaguar, frames the knight's face in the great cat's jaws. Note: See the Maztican Armor sidebar for more information. [Dragon #315 (Maztica – The New (Fantasy)])
Lead-lined Breastplate	PROFICIENCY:ARMOR|Lead-lined Breastplate	TYPE:ArmorProfMedium.ArmorType_Medium.Armor.Medium.Suit.Standard	COST:200	WT:35	ACCHECK:-4	MAXDEX:3	SPELLFAILURE:25	BONUS:COMBAT|AC|5|TYPE=Armor	BONUS:VAR|ArmorCheckPenalty|4	SOURCEPAGE:p.1216	DESC:A thin layer of soft lead added to the interior of this breastplate (and often to a skullcap as well) helps protect the mountain ghosts from divinations and mind-affecting enchantments. This armor provides a +1 circumstance bonus on saving throws made to resist such spells. [Dragon #348 (Class Acts – Mountain Ghosts)]
Gorget	TYPE:Goods.General.Armor Accessory	COST:10	WT:5	SPROP:+10 bonus against strangulation attacks only; -4 penalty on physical actions over a period of time (running, swimming, holding breath).	SOURCEPAGE:p.1216	DESC:A gorget is a metal collar that provides a +10 armor bonus against strangulation attacks. A gorget has hardness 10 and 5 hit points. It must be custom-made for its wearer and imposes a -4 penalty on checks made to perform physical actions over a period of time (running, swimming, breath-holding, and so on). Note: See the "Strangulation" side bar on page 18 for more information on strangulation attacks and weapons. [Dragon #355 (Class Acts: Strangulation)]
Leather Collar	TYPE:Goods.General.Armor Accessory	COST:2	WT:2	SPROP:+4 bonus against strangulation attacks only; -2 penalty on physical actions over a period of time (running, swimming, holding breath).	SOURCEPAGE:p.1216	DESC:This simplified leather gorget provides a +4 armor bonus against strangulation attacks. A leather collar has hardness 3 and 1 hit point. It must he custom-made for its wearer. A leather collar imposes a -2 penalty on checks made to perform physical actions that extend over a period of time. Note: See the "Strangulation" side bar on page 18 for more information on strangulation attacks and weapons. [Dragon #355 (Class Acts: Strangulation)]
